---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const recoverSourceMeaningResult = await recoverSourceMeaning(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const designMappingsResult = await designMappings(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, recoverSourceMeaningResult.accepted);
const resolveRecordsResult = await resolveRecords(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, designMappingsResult.accepted);
const rehearseMigrationResult = await rehearseMigration(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, resolveRecordsResult.accepted);
const coordinateCutoverResult = await coordinateCutover(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, rehearseMigrationResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { recoverSourceMeaning: recoverSourceMeaningResult, designMappings: designMappingsResult, resolveRecords: resolveRecordsResult, rehearseMigration: rehearseMigrationResult, coordinateCutover: coordinateCutoverResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...recoverSourceMeaningResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...designMappingsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...resolveRecordsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...rehearseMigrationResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...coordinateCutoverResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...recoverSourceMeaningResult.checks, ...designMappingsResult.checks, ...resolveRecordsResult.checks, ...rehearseMigrationResult.checks, ...coordinateCutoverResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A source system reuses identifiers: include system and historical validity in identity keys. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (include system and historical validity in identity keys.) through the existing stage result for SourceFieldMeaning; preserve exact source/version and the prior SourceFieldMeaning, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A null has several meanings: preserve explicit missing-state categories in the target. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (preserve explicit missing-state categories in the target.) through the existing stage result for SourceFieldMeaning; preserve exact source/version and the prior SourceFieldMeaning, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — Source data changes during migration: capture and replay deltas against the approved mapping version. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (capture and replay deltas against the approved mapping version.) through the existing stage result for SourceFieldMeaning; preserve exact source/version and the prior SourceFieldMeaning, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A target constraint cannot represent a valid source case: propose a schema extension or quarantine, not fabricated data. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (propose a schema extension or quarantine, not fabricated data.) through the existing stage result for SourceFieldMeaning; preserve exact source/version and the prior SourceFieldMeaning, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — Rollback would overwrite new target work: use an explicit reconciliation plan. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (use an explicit reconciliation plan.) through the existing stage result for SourceFieldMeaning; preserve exact source/version and the prior SourceFieldMeaning, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, recoverSourceMeaning: recoverSourceMeaningResult, designMappings: designMappingsResult, resolveRecords: resolveRecordsResult, rehearseMigration: rehearseMigrationResult, coordinateCutover: coordinateCutoverResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
